<rss version="2.0" xmlns:dc="http://purl.org/dc/elements/1.1/"><channel><title>出版物 |皮尤研究中心</title><link>https://www.pewresearch.org/publications/</link><description>塑造您世界的数字、事实和趋势</description><lastBuildDate>Sat, 01 Aug 2026 05:25:56 GMT</lastBuildDate><generator>rfeed v1.1.1</generator><docs>https://github.com/svpino/rfeed/blob/master/README.md</docs><item><title>大约一半的美国人表示他们在智能手机上花费了太多时间</title><link>https://www.pewresearch.org/short-reads/2026/09/01/about-half-of-americans-say-they-spend-too-much-time-on-their-smartphone/</link><description>&lt;img height="110" src="https://www.pewresearch.org/wp-content/uploads/sites/20/2026/08/SR_26.09.01-phone-screen_featured.jpg?w=194&amp;amp;h=110&amp;amp;crop=1" width="194" /&gt;&lt;br /&gt;&lt;br /&gt;&lt;p&gt;十分之七的 30 岁以下成年人表示，他们在智能手机上花费了太多时间，30 岁至 49 岁的成年人中约有三分之二也是如此。&lt;/p&gt;&lt;br /&gt;&lt;br /&gt; &lt;span style="font-size: 12px; color: gray;"&gt;（使用&lt;a href="https://fetchrss.com/feedLink?w=6a6d836405e2f22d650b3382" target="_blank"&gt;FetchRSS&lt;/a&gt;生成的提要）&lt;/span&gt;</description><pubDate>Wed, 02 Sep 2026 01:45:53 GMT</pubDate><guid isPermaLink="true">https://www.pewresearch.org/short-reads/2026/09/01/about-half-of-americans-say-they-spend-too-much-time-on-their-smartphone/</guid></item><item><title>拉丁美洲人对于美国梦能否实现存在分歧</title><link>https://www.pewresearch.org/race-and-ethnicity/2026/09/01/latinos-are-split-on-whether-the-american-dream-is-achievable/</link><description>&lt;img height="110" src="https://www.pewresearch.org/wp-content/uploads/sites/20/2026/09/RE_2026.09.01_latinos-american-dream_featured.png?w=194&amp;amp;h=110&amp;amp;crop=1" width="194" /&gt;&lt;br /&gt;&lt;br /&gt;&lt;p&gt;更多的拉丁美洲人表示他们的生活水平比父母的好（57%），而不是更差（23%）。更多人还表示，他们的孩子的生活水平将比他们自己的更好（53%），而不是更差（14%）。&lt;/p&gt;&lt;br /&gt;&lt;br /&gt; &lt;span style="font-size: 12px; color: gray;"&gt;（使用&lt;a href="https://fetchrss.com/feedLink?w=6a6d836405e2f22d650b3382" target="_blank"&gt;FetchRSS&lt;/a&gt;生成的提要）&lt;/span&gt;</description><pubDate>Wed, 02 Sep 2026 01:45:53 GMT</pubDate><guid isPermaLink="true">https://www.pewresearch.org/race-and-ethnicity/2026/09/01/latinos-are-split-on-whether-the-american-dream-is-achievable/</guid></item><item><title>谁认为自己是工人阶级？</title><link>https://www.pewresearch.org/politics/2026/08/31/who-sees-themselves-as-working-class/</link><description>&lt;img height="110" src="https://www.pewresearch.org/wp-content/uploads/sites/20/2026/08/PP_2026.8.31_working-class_featured.png?w=194&amp;amp;h=110&amp;amp;crop=1" width="194" /&gt;&lt;br /&gt;&lt;br /&gt;&lt;p&gt;大多数美国人认为自己是工人阶级，共和党人比民主党人更有可能这样做。&lt;/p&gt;&lt;br /&gt;&lt;br /&gt; &lt;span style="font-size: 12px; color: gray;"&gt;（使用&lt;a href="https://fetchrss.com/feedLink?w=6a6d836405e2f22d650b3382" target="_blank"&gt;FetchRSS&lt;/a&gt;生成的提要）&lt;/span&gt;</description><pubDate>Wed, 02 Sep 2026 01:45:53 GMT</pubDate><guid isPermaLink="true">https://www.pewresearch.org/politics/2026/08/31/who-sees-themselves-as-working-class/</guid></item><item><title>国际社会对美国及其总统的看法越来越相关</title><link>https://www.pewresearch.org/decoded/2026/08/28/international-views-of-the-us-and-its-president-are-increasingly-correlated/</link><description>&lt;img height="110" src="https://www.pewresearch.org/wp-content/uploads/sites/20/2026/08/d_26.08.28_pres_us_correlated_crop.png?w=194&amp;amp;h=110&amp;amp;crop=1" width="194" /&gt;&lt;br /&gt;&lt;br /&gt;&lt;p&gt;在乔·拜登担任总统期间以及唐纳德·特朗普的第一个任期内，对美国的看法与对总统的信心之间的关系要弱得多。&lt;/p&gt;&lt;br /&gt;&lt;br /&gt; &lt;span style="font-size: 12px; color: gray;"&gt;（使用&lt;a href="https://fetchrss.com/feedLink?w=6a6d836405e2f22d650b3382" target="_blank"&gt;FetchRSS&lt;/a&gt;生成的提要）&lt;/span&gt;</description><pubDate>Sun, 30 Aug 2026 02:09:09 GMT</pubDate><guid isPermaLink="true">https://www.pewresearch.org/decoded/2026/08/28/international-views-of-the-us-and-its-president-are-increasingly-correlated/</guid></item><item><title>超过一半的 40 多岁美国人夹在年迈的父母和自己的孩子之间</title><link>https://www.pewresearch.org/short-reads/2026/08/27/more-than-half-of-americans-in-their-40s-are-sandwiched-between-an-aging-parent-and-their-own-children/</link><description>&lt;img height="110" src="https://www.pewresearch.org/wp-content/uploads/sites/20/2022/04/FT_22.04.01_SandwichGeneration_feature.jpg?w=194&amp;amp;h=110&amp;amp;crop=1" width="194" /&gt;&lt;br /&gt;&lt;br /&gt;&lt;p&gt;总体而言，25% 的美国成年人的父母年龄在 65 岁或以上，并且有一个 18 岁以下的孩子、一个接受经济支持的成年孩子或两者兼而有之。&lt;/p&gt;&lt;br /&gt;&lt;br /&gt; &lt;span style="font-size: 12px; color: gray;"&gt;（使用&lt;a href="https://fetchrss.com/feedLink?w=6a6d836405e2f22d650b3382" target="_blank"&gt;FetchRSS&lt;/a&gt;生成的提要）&lt;/span&gt;</description><pubDate>Thu, 27 Aug 2026 21:23:39 GMT</pubDate><guid isPermaLink="true">https://www.pewresearch.org/short-reads/2026/08/27/more-than-half-of-americans-in-their-40s-are-sandwiched-between-an-aging-parent-and-their-own-children/</guid></item></channel></rss>